# Subagent Council Loop & Report Protocol (MANDATORY — NOT GAUNTLET)

**NOT:** Gauntlet loop · gauntlet-critic · BAR · scores · "make gate green."

**Full docs:** `docs/qa/SUBAGENT_COUNCIL_LOOP.md` · `docs/qa/COUNCIL_REPORT_MANDATE.md` · `docs/qa/COUNCIL_AUDIT_LOG.md`

Do **not** apply gameplay, planning, or SSOT fixes until the council passes. Every report that claims a fix or progress on gameplay/planning/combat **MUST show what changed AND per-critic PASS proof recorded BEFORE apply.** No exceptions.

Headline QA delta without proof table = **invalid report**. "6/6 PASS" without critic rows = **forgery**.

---

## The Non-Negotiable Order

```
PROPOSE → COUNCIL (parallel, all PASS) → REPORT WITH PROOF → APPLY → VERIFY → COMMIT → REPORT AGAIN
```

| Step | Forbidden |
|---|---|
| Apply code before council proof table in chat | **Instant violation** |
| Commit before council proof table in chat | **Instant violation** |
| "6/6 PASS" / "council approved" without per-critic lines | **Invalid report** |
| "Logged post-verify" / council after commit | **Invalid — treat as unauthorized** |
| Headline = QA FAIL count only | **Invalid — proof block must come first** |

Any FAIL → revise proposal → new council. Do not apply partial fixes from critics.
Any code change after council PASS → **amendment council** on full delta before layer DONE.

---

## Council Size & Critic Charters

| Scope | Critics |
|---|---|
| **Default** planning / paint / commit / hover | **5 parallel** (Critics 1–5) |
| + QA FAIL / test edits | **+ Critic 6** (QA-fix discipline) |
| + Class factory / skills | **+ Critic 7** (Class / skill scope) |

Launch all in **one message**. Verdict: **all PASS** (5/5, 6/6, or 7/7). Subagent: **generalPurpose** with charter from doc. **Not** `gauntlet-critic`.

### Critic Charters Summary:
1. **Bible paint & tiles (HARSH):** Range selectability parity (all red legal tiles selectable, no ∅), locked vs bundle (EX-LOCKED-FIELD), path vs flood, EX-BIBLE-UI, behavioral tests in proposal.
2. **Settle / bundle / commit (HARSH):** Move preview persistence across commit until execution phase (no vanishing routes/ghosts), no waypoint wiping on adjacent destinations, Director + Simulator owners, ratify, no post-process redo, EX-FROZEN-REPLAY, EX-PERF-SCHED at flush.
3. **Stand & range origins:** Phase-entry, two-range model, EX-POSTMOVE-SLOT. Red tiles paint from latest committed stand, never turn-start base_board.
4. **Global systems & anti-heuristic:** 6-row audit, exception IDs cited correctly, no silent bypass, no bandaids.
5. **Perf & scheduling:** EX-PERF-SCHED guardian; cheap-walk slot parity; locked paint stable under throttle.
6. *(Optional)* **QA-fix discipline:** `global-systems-first.mdc` § QA Fix Discipline — no overlay fallbacks, no synthetic stand truth, no per-test branches.
7. *(Optional)* **Class / skill scope:** `global-systems-first.mdc` § Skill Global Rules Mandate — abilities follow shared systems; warn owner before any exception.

Each critic returns **PASS/FAIL + rule or exception ID cites only**. No numerical scores.

---

## Mandatory Report Block Format (Every Gameplay Fix Turn)

Use **exact section titles** in owner-facing reply **and** `## Changelog`:

### 1. What we are fixing
- **Bucket / symptom:** (test names or owner symptom — one line)
- **Canonical owner:** (one system/API — not a file alone)
- **Broken step:** (one sentence — what step in owner chain failed)
- **Planned delta:** (files + functions; before → after behavior in plain language)

### 2. Council proof (before apply)

| Critic | Rule / Charter | Focus | Verdict | Proof / Cite |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **1. Bible paint & tiles** | `move-preview-intent-truth` | Range parity & selectable tiles | **PASS** | (exact cite/reason) |
| **2. Settle & commit** | `move-preview-intent-truth` | Preview persistence across commit | **PASS** | (exact cite/reason) |
| **3. Stand origin** | `action-range-latest-stand` | Phase-entry stand tracking | **PASS** | (exact cite/reason) |
| **4. Global systems** | `global-systems-first` | 6-row audit compliance | **PASS** | (exact cite/reason) |
| **5. Perf & frame budget** | `performance-standards` | 60+ FPS throttle stability | **PASS** | (exact cite/reason) |
| **6. QA discipline** | `global-systems-first` | Upstream owner fix, no fallbacks | **PASS** | (exact cite/reason) |
| **7. Class scope** | `class-qa-standards` | Shared systems, no per-skill hack | **PASS** | (exact cite/reason) |

*(Include conversation/subagent ID links or exact log verification).*
